---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Odoo-specific lint checks with project context

Usage: odx lint [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments:
  [PATHS]...
          Files and directories to lint [default: the project's own addons, else the current directory]

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

      --only-changed
          Lint only the addons with changes against `--base`, committed or not

      --base <REF>
          What `--only-changed` compares with [default: the branch's upstream, else `origin/HEAD`]

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

      --fix
          Apply odoo-lint's safe fixes

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only. Only network calls are skipped: local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --unsafe-fixes
          Apply unsafe fixes too

      --diff
          Show the fixes as a diff instead of applying them

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --output-format <FORMAT>
          Output format of the findings

          Possible values:
          - text:   pylint-style `path:line:col: CODE: message (name)`
          - json:   JSON array, 1-based line and column
          - github: GitHub Actions workflow commands, shown as annotations on pull requests
          - sarif:  SARIF 2.1.0, for GitHub code scanning, reviewdog (Forgejo, Gitea) and IDEs
          - gitlab: GitLab Code Quality report, shown in merge requests
          
          [default: text]

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --select <RULES>
          Rules to check instead of the configured ones (codes, names or code prefixes)

      --ignore <RULES>
          Rules to leave out on top of the configured ones

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

      --exit-zero
          Exit 0 even when findings are left

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
